# JetKVM Mini (the Ethernet model)
#
# Build it with:
#   idf.py -B build.jetkvm_mini -D SDKCONFIG=build.jetkvm_mini/sdkconfig \
#     -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;boards/jetkvm_mini.defaults" build
#
# A small finished box from JetKVM on an ESP32-P4X (rev 3.x, 32 MB PSRAM) with
# 16 MB of flash, a TC358743 HDMI bridge, 100M Ethernet, a microSD slot, a
# 240x240 colour screen on top and two buttons on a side, in a 42 x 42 x 23 mm box. Every pin below is taken
# from JetKVM's own open firmware (github.com/jetkvm/mini, MIT):
#   Capture: TC358743 on I2C0, SDA 2, SCL 5, address 0x0f, RESETN 32, INT 33,
#            two CSI lanes, a 27 MHz oscillator. LDO3 at 2.5 V feeds both the
#            oscillator and the MIPI PHY, and the capture code turns it on
#            before it probes the bridge, as on every other board.
#   Ethernet: IP101 at address 1, reset on 51, the RMII pins ESP-IDF uses by
#            default - the firmware's defaults, pin for pin.
#   microSD: CLK 43, CMD 44, D0-D3 39-42. Card detect on 45 (low with a card
#            in), power through a P-channel MOSFET on 46 (low is on), and the
#            IO rail (VDD_IO_5) on LDO4 at 3.3 V.
#   Screen:  ST7789 on SPI2 at 20 MHz, MOSI 3, SCLK 13, DC 20, RST 21, CS 22,
#            backlight 4. 240x240 of glass on a 240x320 controller, colours
#            inverted, RGB order.
#   Buttons: SW2 on 47 and SW3 on 23, active low behind 10K pull-ups. SW2 is
#            the button for the password reset here.
#   Log:     USB Serial/JTAG on the EXT port (GPIO 24/25). There is no UART
#            bridge on the board.
#
# How to get it on (the stock firmware is GPG-signed and will not take ours):
# check the eFuses first (espefuse.py summary: no Secure Boot, no flash
# encryption), turn on "USB debugging" in JetKVM's own settings so the EXT
# port stays a USB Serial/JTAG, back up the whole flash with
# `esptool read_flash 0 0x1000000` (JetKVM also publishes a recovery image) -
# and flash over the EXT port.
#
# NOT YET RUN ON THE DEVICE. Configured from JetKVM's source and published so
# owners can try it.

# --- flash and partitions ---------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_PARTITION_TABLE_CUSTOM_FILENAME="partitions_16mb.csv"

# --- silicon revision -------------------------------------------------------
# ESP32-P4X only, so there is no pre-3.0 twin.
CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=n
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_300=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_250M=y

# --- updates ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_UPDATE_URL="https://fw.espkvm.io/firmware/jetkvm-mini/manifest.json"

# --- capture ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_I2C_SDA_GPIO=2
CONFIG_KVM_I2C_SCL_GPIO=5
CONFIG_KVM_TC358743_RST_GPIO=32
CONFIG_KVM_BRIDGE_INT_GPIO=33

# --- microSD ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_SD_PWR_GPIO=46
CONFIG_KVM_SD_PWR_ACTIVE_LOW=y
CONFIG_KVM_SD_CD_GPIO=45
CONFIG_KVM_SD_CD_ACTIVE_HIGH=n

# --- button -----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_KVM_BUTTON_GPIO=47

# --- screen -----------------------------------------------------------------
# On from the first boot: the panel is built in.
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_DEFAULT_ON=y
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_DEFAULT_TYPE=15
CONFIG_KVM_GC9A01_SPI_HOST=2
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_MOSI_GPIO=3
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_SCLK_GPIO=13
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_DC_GPIO=20
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_RST_GPIO=21
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_CS_GPIO=22
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_BL_GPIO=4
# Built in: Settings offers on/off, upside down and the brightness, not the
# type or the pins. JetKVM's own default is 15 %; a little more reads better.
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_FIXED=y
CONFIG_KVM_DISP_BRIGHT_DEFAULT=40

# --- the second button ------------------------------------------------------
# SW3 is button 1 in Settings, Buttons: a short press shows the
# next status page, holding it turns the screen off or on. Both can be
# changed there, to the target's power button for one.
CONFIG_KVM_BTN_COUNT=1
CONFIG_KVM_BTN1_FIXED=y
CONFIG_KVM_BTN_GPIO_DEFAULT=23
CONFIG_KVM_BTN_PRESS_DEFAULT=11
CONFIG_KVM_BTN_HOLD_DEFAULT=12

# --- what the box does not have ---------------------------------------------
# No pins come out of it, so the add-ons wired to GPIOs (ATX, a UART serial
# console, a clock module) fold away in Settings, and so does the Pins tab.
# The serial port over the target's USB cable still works.
CONFIG_KVM_BOARD_NO_FREE_GPIO=y
# The TC358743's audio lines are not wired to the P4 on this board, so sound
# comes only as the USB speaker (Settings > Audio > Sound over USB).

# --- console ----------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_USB_SERIAL_JTAG=y

# Which board this is: names it in the console.
CONFIG_KVM_BOARD_JETKVM_MINI=y
